# Venting Architecture (mirror Zalleon)

Reference project: `/Users/abdulrahman/development/projects/Zalleon`

Always match Zalleon’s layering, naming, and dependency flow. Do **not** call APIs from UI, BLoCs, or widgets directly.

## Required flow for every API / business action

```
API DTO (domain/data/api)
  → Repository (domain/repository)
    → Usecase (domain/usecase)
      → Bloc (presentation/.../bloc)
        → Screen / widgets
```

| Layer | Path | Responsibility |
|-------|------|----------------|
| DTO / models | `lib/domain/data/api/` | freezed + json_serializable response/request models |
| App models | `lib/domain/data/app/` | Domain models not tied to one API shape |
| Exceptions | `lib/domain/data/exceptions/` | e.g. `MainAPIException` |
| Repository | `lib/domain/repository/api/` (or `app/`) | Extends `BaseRepository`; talks to `api_client`; returns `TaskEither` |
| Usecase | `lib/domain/usecase/` | One class per use case; depends on repository; returns `TaskEither` |
| Bloc | `lib/presentation/<feature>/bloc/` | Calls usecases only; freezed events/states |
| DI | `lib/di/venting_module_extensions/` | Register repo → usecase → bloc |

## Rules

1. **Never** put HTTP/`apiClient` calls in a Bloc, screen, or widget.
2. **Never** skip the usecase (Bloc must not depend on Repository directly).
3. One repository method / class per API concern; one usecase class per business action.
4. Prefer `fpdart` `TaskEither` in repository and usecase; map failures to `MainAPIException`.
5. Register new repos in `venting_module_repositories.dart`, usecases in the usecases module, blocs in `venting_module_blocs.dart`.
6. Feature UI lives under `lib/presentation/<feature>/` with colocated `bloc/` and `widgets/`.
7. When unsure, copy the nearest equivalent pattern from Zalleon (`LoginRepository` → `LoginUsecase` → feature Bloc).

## Example (Zalleon-style)

```dart
// repository
class LoginRepository extends BaseRepository {
  TaskEither<Exception, LoginResponseModel> call({...}) => executeRequest(...);
}

// usecase
class LoginUsecase {
  final LoginRepository loginRepository;
  TaskEither<Exception, LoginResponseModel> call({...}) =>
      loginRepository.call(...);
}

// bloc — injects LoginUsecase only, not the repository
```

## Forbidden

- Calling Dio/`ApiClient` from presentation
- Fat repositories with unrelated endpoints dumped together without clear grouping
- Business logic only in the Bloc with no usecase
- Inventing a different folder layout than Zalleon for the same concern
